  "finalText": "Now the idle wiggle on the whole lockup, then a check of the frames.\nI built the \"Boop!\" intro on the 1080×1080, 5 s comp, on a deep navy background (#2B2D42) with a candy palette.\n\n- **Candy drop (0–1.0 s):** Six shapes (pink circle, yellow star, sky rounded square, mint circle, violet star, pink rounded square) fall in from above, staggered 0.1 s apart. Each one stretches on the way down, squashes on landing and bounces back up.\n- **Jostle (1.45–2.4 s):** The shapes nudge sideways into each other and settle with a little spring.\n- **Letters hop (2.5–3.9 s):** B-o-o-p-! rise from below one at a time, 0.12 s apart. Each one launches with a stretch, lands with a squash and gives a small trampoline bounce. Each letter has its own colour.\n- **Idle wiggle (4.2–5.0 s):** The whole lockup sways about ±3° with decaying ease-in-out and ends on its resting pose.\n\nEverything sits in one group, **Boop intro**, so the wiggle moves the whole lockup. The frame check on the contact sheet looks clean.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- Colours: the background and palette are my picks, not a brand spec. Tell me the brand colours and I'll swap them in.\n- Font: the text uses Inter Black. A rounder kids' face such as Nunito would feel more playful if it's available.\n- Easing: I used Back Out and spring:0.35 for the bounces rather than true spring physics.\n\nI can add a sound family or tune the bounce heights if you want it bouncier."
